# The NOTES panel (src/notes.zig): `<ws>/.mnml/notes/*.md`, one row per
# note as `<name>  <title>  <age>`, the shared `sort:` chip, and `n`
# seeding the next free `note-N.md`.
write .mnml/notes/note-1.md "# Ship it\n\nbody\n"
write .mnml/notes/ideas.md "loose thought\n"
command view.activity_notes
# The panel lives on the left (Rust's placement) in the tree's 30
# columns, where the header keeps only the chips' icons; drag the
# column's divider out to 60 so the rows read in full.
drag 30 5 60 5
wait 400
expect screen contains NOTES
expect screen contains "sort: Newest first"
expect screen contains "note-1  Ship it"
expect screen contains "ideas  loose thought"
# The filter narrows by name and title.
key /
type ship
expect screen contains "(1 of 2)"
expect screen lacks "loose thought"
key esc
key esc
expect screen contains "loose thought"
# The sort chip cycles.
command notes.sort
expect screen contains "sort: Oldest first"
# `n` seeds the next free name; enter creates and opens it.
key n
expect screen contains "note-2.md"
key enter
expect pane note-2.md
expect file .mnml/notes/note-2.md lacks "zzz"
